{
  "id": "neo-spring-road-2001",
  "name": "Neo Spring Road 2001",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "Pokémon Card Battle★Neo Spring Road was Japan's spring tournament circuit of 2001, in seven regions from Kyoto on 11 February to Hiroshima on 25 March 2001, with branding themed on Lugia. The top three of each tournament won No. 1, No. 2 or No. 3 Trainer cards. Its trophy cards keep Ken Sugimori's art from 2000's World Challenge cards, in a boy's and a girl's version, with more Pokémon the higher the place, but their text names only the event, not the junior or senior division. Each winner's name, tournament, division and place were printed above the picture, and the card came in an acrylic trophy case. Spare copies with nothing printed above the picture, probably straight from the printer, have since turned up. The winners' list in Trainers magazine shows one girl among its 72 winners, a third-place finisher.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Pokumon: Pokémon Card Battle Neo Spring / Summer Road 2001",
        "url": "https://pokumon.com/pokemon-card-battle-neo-spring-summer-road-2001/"
      },
      {
